{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If a woman conceives.</b> Rabbi Simlai said: Just as man's formation was after every beast, animal, and bird in the work of Creation, so his Torah was set forth after the Torah of beast, animal, and bird (Leviticus Rabbah 14)." "<b>If she conceives.</b> To include even if she gave birth to a מָחוּי — that was smudged and made like a form of seed — her mother is impure with childbirth impurity (Niddah 27)." "<b>As the days of the impurity of her menstruation shall she be impure.</b> After the order of every impurity stated regarding a menstruating woman, she becomes impure with childbirth impurity — and even if the womb opened without blood (ibid. 21)." "<b>Of her menstruation.</b> A term for something flowing from her body. Another interpretation: a term of illness and sickness — for a woman does not see blood without becoming ill, and her head and limbs grow heavy upon her (ibid. 9)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:03.416521352Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}